2️⃣ Why Java 8 Date-Time classes are thread-safe?
Java 8 Date-Time classes are thread-safe because they are immutable—once created, their state cannot be modified,
so multiple threads can safely share them without synchronization.

🧠 Why immutability = thread safety
Example:
LocalDate d = LocalDate.now();
d.plusDays(1);

plusDays() does not modify d
It returns a new object
So:
No shared mutable state
No race condition
No synchronization needed

🔑 Interview one-liner (memorize)
“Java 8 date-time classes are thread-safe because they are immutable and have no shared mutable state.”

